From cf2a18ffe28848a51aa05b1f92288e53ed224a67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:17:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Make self-registration independent of Supabase's built-in
 mailer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root-cause fixes for the two issues hit today (a corrupted
VITE_SUPABASE_URL causing ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED, and a confirmation
e-mail whose link went nowhere):

- src/lib/config.js and api/_lib.js now validate the Supabase project
  URL shape at startup and fail loudly to the console instead of
  silently sending every request to a broken host.
- /register no longer calls supabase.auth.signUp() from the browser,
  which was at the mercy of the dashboard's "Confirm email" toggle and
  its own unbranded e-mail/redirect handling. It now posts to the new
  api/register.js, which uses the admin API directly:
    * REQUIRE_EMAIL_CONFIRMATION unset/"false" (today's setup):
      the account is created already confirmed, no e-mail involved,
      the client signs the person straight in.
    * REQUIRE_EMAIL_CONFIRMATION="true" (future option): the account
      is created unconfirmed and we send our own Hornung-branded
      confirmation e-mail (same Resend pattern as client invites),
      with a redirect computed from PUBLIC_SITE_URL server-side —
      never Supabase's default template or Site URL setting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ici8AbYj73icYwNgUinzM
---
 .env.example           |   6 ++
 api/_lib.js            |  19 ++++++-
 api/register.js        | 125 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/lib/config.js      |  26 ++++++++-
 src/pages/Register.jsx |  53 ++++++++++-------
 5 files changed, 205 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 api/register.js

